      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/263c58a4250424e5dd87e991e2d2d87656c1fa08d10cfc178637d44d63414423.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?",
      "worked_solution": "The red rays contain all values less than $-2$ or greater than $2.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $-2$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $-2,$ and\n\n- the open circle at $2$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $2.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<-2$ or $x>2.$",
