      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/264828b133192b7fff74cfef0718ec56cf82d638003bb9774c2318cb3ae2cc2c.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}\n$1\\text{ or }x$\n{{field-2}}$4.$",
      "worked_solution": "The red rays contain all values less than $1$ or greater than $4.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $1,$ and\n\n- the closed circle at $4$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<1$ or $x\\ge 4.$",
