      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $-4\\le x\\le 0?$",
      "worked_solution": "The inequality $-4\\le x\\le 0$ means that $x$ can take any value greater than or equal to $-4,$ and less than or equal to $0.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we draw a closed circle at $-4$ and another closed circle at $0.$ Then, we highlight the region between the points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/e884f5bcda9ad664f00a59c8bffcd72ce21472b2cb9127c26ad5cdbd42c73fc5.png)",
