    "q-54811": {
      "dom_id": "step-q54811",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/2ac03455fb1b259e0f31719c613d9f7c3adb50b7d8e96667514abb7c513ed0e3.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?",
      "worked_solution": "The red segment contains all values between  $-1$ and $4.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $4$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-1\\le x\\le 4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
