      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151668/assets/945f83a6af821028b133995ddc13193b325ce9cea7d97c8617532369b570542e.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $-1${{field-1}}\n$x$\n{{field-2}}$3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The red segment contains all values between  $-1$ and $3.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $3$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $3.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-1\\le x\\le 3.$",
